		<Item class="StringValue" referent="RBX31">
			<Properties>
				<string name="Name">HOW_TO_USE</string>
				<string name="Value">HORROR MONSTER CHASE AI - PATROL / SIGHT + PROXIMITY / CHASE / SEARCH / HIDE

SETUP (no code):
1. Put 'MonsterEvent', 'MonsterSync' and the 'Config' folder in game.ReplicatedStorage.
2. Put the 'Waypoints' and 'HideSpots' folders in game.Workspace - drag their markers to lay out
   the patrol route (its markers hide themselves while the game runs) and the spots
   players can hide at.
3. Put 'MonsterServer' Script (it carries MonsterAdmin + MonsterCaught) in game.ServerScriptService.
4. Put 'MonsterClient' LocalScript in game.StarterPlayer.StarterPlayerScripts.
5. Press Play. A red placeholder monster patrols the waypoints and hunts you.

HOW IT HUNTS: it walks the waypoint loop (PATROL). It CHASES anyone it sees inside its sight cone
with a clear line of view, or senses within close range. Lose it (break line of sight, get far, or
HIDE at a hide-spot) and it heads to where it last saw you (SEARCH), then goes back to patrol. Get
caught and it triggers a jumpscare + the MonsterCaught event (by default the caught player resets).
Entering/leaving a chase fires a music cue on the client (set ChaseMusic.SoundId to your track).

TUNE (no code): the Config NumberValues - sight range/angle, hearing radius, patrol/chase/search
speeds, lose + search time, catch range, hide radius. USE YOUR OWN MONSTER: add a Model (with at
least one Part) named 'MonsterRig' under MonsterServer to replace the placeholder. DRIVE from your code:
    game.ServerScriptService.MonsterServer.MonsterAdmin:Fire('forcechase', player)
    game.ServerScriptService.MonsterServer.MonsterCaught.Event:Connect(function(plr) ... end)

SESSION only - stateless between servers by design. No external services. Delete this note.</string>
			</Properties>
		</Item>
	</Item>
